    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d702">

                <pb facs="0742" n="692" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg692"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1894-04-02"><hi rendition="#italic">April 2,
                                1894</hi></date>. (Received April 21.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 221.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    court for the correction of errors at Bagdad has found that the evidence taken
                    in the case pending lately at Mosul, for the assault on Miss Melton, was
                    sufficient to justify the conviction of eight of the twelve men found guilty by
                    the trial court, and not sufficient for the conviction of the other four. * *
                    *</p>
                <pb facs="0743" n="693" xml:id="pg693"/>
                <p>This information I derive from the grand vizier. The case goes back for final
                    judgment by the trial court, and the result as to the punishment inflicted will
                    soon be known.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
